WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.420
- Hey, my name is Ben Schwartz.

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:06.100
I'm here at BuzzFeed to talk
about my new film, Blue Iguana

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.420
with Sam Rockwell, coming
everywhere August 24th

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:10.143
and it, my friends,

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:13.200
is time to S some T

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.390
which means spill some tea.

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:15.440
Shall we?
(upbeat music)

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:16.313
Watch as I do it.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:17.423
Hold.

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:21.040
Whenever you pour tea, gently cradle,

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.140
I call this the armpit

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:27.293
and as high as you can go
and as slow as you can go.

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:28.243
Join me.

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:31.310
I feel like when we look back at the show,

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:34.940
the writing staff of
that show is so strong.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:37.590
If you look at it it's
like the best writers

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:39.030
and so when we got scripts it was always

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.140
the funniest thing I'd ever read

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.430
so we would always do it as is,

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:44.370
and I'll play a little
bit and then many times

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:45.650
we'll do something called
a fun run at the end

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:47.190
where you can kind of go nuts.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:48.330
We got what we needed, go nuts.

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:49.890
Sometimes they keep some of
that, sometimes they don't

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:51.560
but the words were always great.

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:53.140
That show, the writers on that show,

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.630
it's a very special, special thing.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.080
It was a really special show.

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:58.710
Jean-Ralphio and I have
many traits in common.

00:00:58.710 --> 00:00:59.810
We have the same hair.

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:02.530
Anytime I played Jean-Ralphio
I would grow out my hair

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:04.760
as long as I could so when it came time,

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:07.133
I looked as stupid as I could.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:08.484
Me and the hair and make up people

00:01:08.484 --> 00:01:10.946
had like the best time making me look

00:01:10.946 --> 00:01:14.868
like a crazy cartoon character
every time we did it.

00:01:14.868 --> 00:01:15.860
(lighthearted music)

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:17.660
I would probably want
to switch with Pratt,

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:19.770
Pratt or Perd Hapley.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:21.840
And I could never do Nick
Offerman's character,

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:24.320
he's just too perfect, like
I wouldn't be able to do it.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.990
Yeah, I think I'd probably
say Pratt or Perd Hapley.

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:28.850
Perd Hapley is one of
my favorite characters

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:30.350
on all of television. (laughing)

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:34.033
I think he's so funny,
I think he's so funny.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.030
I'm trying to think, most
of scenes were with Aziz

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.400
and he's incredibly funny.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.750
Jenny really made me laugh.

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:42.003
Jenny's so funny, Jenny
really made me laugh.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:43.980
Pratt, Pratt makes me laugh.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:45.420
I don't know about cracking up on the spot

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:47.360
but anytime anybody improvised I would go,

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:49.200
it would make me so happy but oftentimes

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.230
when I'm in a scene, I'm the crazy person

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:52.600
and the the other
person's the straight man

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.540
because my character was
so insane. (laughing)

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.780
Everybody there, I'm talking
about like Retta, Jim,

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:01.540
everybody there, Amy is
obviously an icon, a legend.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:03.110
They're all incredibly
funny, I don't remember,

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:04.650
I'm sure all of them made
me laugh at some time

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:07.150
because they're just amazing,
they're truly amazing.

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:08.410
I love those guys so much.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:09.910
Can I say something about tea?

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:12.670
I do love tea and one of
the reasons why I love it

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:15.123
is that it's delicious, it's classy.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.460
I mean, it's really hard to

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:20.230
know how much I enjoy it

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:23.393
until I really pour myself a
good cuppa, a good cuppa tea.

00:02:23.414 --> 00:02:24.500
(playful music)

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:26.963
Yeah, one of my favorite
Jean-Ralphio lines is,

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:29.573
we're exiting a car,
we're exiting in a van,

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:32.390
it was after that episode where Nick

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:33.910
is dancing like this with a tiny hat

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:34.940
where everybody's drinking Snake Juice

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:36.510
and it's a very small line,

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.190
we're leaving and I'm in the back

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:41.010
and as the car pulls
away everybody's laughing

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:44.190
and as they pull away I go,
"I'm so alone." (laughing)

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:46.180
That's it, it's such a small line

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.906
and I can't believe it
made the cut. (laughing)

00:02:48.906 --> 00:02:52.823
(people laughing)
I'm so alone.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:56.440
I mean Don Cheadle to me, listen,

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:59.466
to be that good, he's such a good actor.

00:02:59.466 --> 00:03:01.430
Cheadle's incredible, you what it is?

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:03.633
Kristen Bell like treated us like,

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:06.400
she was so incredible
and then took care of us

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:09.140
and then while she was
going that she had two kids

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.870
so like she was able to do everything

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:15.150
and manage everything and
then take care of us as well

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:16.020
which is incredible.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:18.632
And Cheadle, man, you
just, it's like everyday

00:03:18.632 --> 00:03:20.306
is like class, you could just sit back

00:03:20.306 --> 00:03:23.129
and watch one of the
greatest actors of all time

00:03:23.129 --> 00:03:25.984
do what he does and
also you gain confidence

00:03:25.984 --> 00:03:27.848
because when you're in scenes with him,

00:03:27.848 --> 00:03:30.750
you create with him and you
create something together

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:34.688
and so it's very exciting to
be around both of those people

00:03:34.688 --> 00:03:36.463
for those reasons.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.720
Can you guys be honest,
do I drink tea weird?

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:42.965
Because I'll so this in
a restaurant and be like.

00:03:42.965 --> 00:03:45.600
I just like to get it on
the very ends of my lips.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:47.218
(sipping tea)

00:03:47.218 --> 00:03:48.483
(upbeat music)

00:03:48.483 --> 00:03:50.803
I don't know, what do people
say about me? (laughing)

00:03:50.803 --> 00:03:52.727
I don't know, what's happening?

00:03:53.091 --> 00:03:55.230
Um, sometimes people will think

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:56.430
that I'm very much like Jean-Ralphio

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:57.844
because I played him or
that I'm a little bit

00:03:57.844 --> 00:03:59.760
of a douche bag because of Jean-Ralphio

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.943
but I'm very much not like that.

00:04:02.029 --> 00:04:04.270
I actually don't really get to go to clubs

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:05.770
or anything like that usually.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:08.740
Oh yeah, this is some
mess, this is a mess.

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:10.370
What a mistake, and I stained my clothes

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:11.400
and I got more press today.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.068
I can Venmo you for the rug, I think.

00:04:13.068 --> 00:04:15.390
If I wanted to switch
characters with anybody

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:16.960
for a day, what would it be?

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:20.550
It is easy, it would probably
be either Sonic the Hedgehog

00:04:20.572 --> 00:04:21.690
or Dewey Duck.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:25.280
First of all, if I'm Sonic,
I can run as fast as anybody

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.580
and I'm also a hedgehog
and I guess I love rings

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:29.943
so I'm very into that.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.500
It probably would be Sonic,
how could would that be?

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:33.743
I can turn into a ball.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:35.273
What are you crazy?

00:04:35.273 --> 00:04:36.203
I would love that!

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:39.250
The process of me getting
Sonic was a long one,

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:41.270
a really long one, it started a year ago.

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:42.103
Where was I?

00:04:42.103 --> 00:04:43.510
I think the director, Jeff, called me

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:47.320
and he said that, "The role is yours."

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.393
I did like a Tiger Woods one of these,

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:50.500
I went, "Yeah!"

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:52.780
like fist pumped and then looked around

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:53.633
because I was out in the open.

00:04:53.633 --> 00:04:55.670
That one was a, I put in a
lot of work to get that one,

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:57.620
I really wanted it so I
was very, very excited.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:59.445
Hey my name is Ben Schwartz and I am still

00:04:59.445 --> 00:05:00.860
at BuzzFeed.
(lighthearted music)

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:01.950
This has been so much fun.

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:04.110
Listen, we spilled some tea literally.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:05.230
Check me out with Sam Rockwell

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:07.453
in a movie called Blue
Iguana, August 24th.

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:09.940
It is gonna be on SVOD which I think means

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:13.283
everywhere that you can
download things on demand?

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.543
I'm assuming?

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:17.100
And then it's gonna be in
theaters as well, same time

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:18.630
and Sam Rockwell just won an Oscar

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.484
so I mean like, there's way
more pressure for him than me.

00:05:21.484 --> 00:05:24.623
Enjoy the movie. (laughing)

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.940
This is the most serious
interview I've done,

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:28.390
no joke, you can ask them.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:30.640
Every other interview
has been me going crazy

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:32.590
and it's at BuzzFeed
which seems like the place

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:34.240
that you would go the most crazy.

00:05:36.344 --> 00:05:40.100
(dry erase marker squeaking on whiteboard)

